  "deviations": [
    "The scanned page is a picture in the app; the artboard draws it as typed text. The harness serves a blank page picture of the same size (fixtures/blank-page.svg) and hides the artboard's page text, so only the paper box and the highlight are compared (fonts, padding and colour of the paper are not).",
    "Toolbar chips are drawn 44px high as in the canvas; their tap area stays 52px through an ::after hit box. Links such as 'Change a detail' and 'Why we do this' keep a 52px tap area the same way.",
    "The canvas source line reads 'GP record \u00b7 consultations'; the API gives a page's source type only, so the page shows 'GP record'. The words after the dot need a page-section field.",
    "'Not right' for a checked fact is a quiet link that appears on the checked row when pointed at, tapped or reached by keyboard (the canvas draws no button there; the server allows it).",
    "'Also: R mark as read, 3 change a detail, J and K change page' is kept for screen readers only; the canvas draws just the three key hints.",
    "'Add a reason' (optional reason for Not right) sits beside 'Change a detail' on one line; the canvas has no such control.",
    "The first 'PLEASE CHECK' card shows no kind label ('Consultation'); it stays in the page for screen readers.",
    "The Examination value is not bold when 'None recorded': the canvas emphasis is a content rule the API does not carry.",
    "The header's step pills sit a few pixels from the canvas (case bar is foundation-owned, not changed here).",
    "The page keeps the reader's suggestion switcher: one full card at a time, then the switcher list and 'Checked on this page (n)' folded below it. The canvas stacks the card, a checked row and a flag button, so the 'checked row' and 'flag button' probes are dropped (they are still built and tested in the card of a checked suggestion) and the keyboard hints sit higher (rect.y allowed on 'keys')."
  ],
  "artboardCss": "[style*='min-height: 560px'] > div:not([style*='FFF3B0']){visibility:hidden} [style*='min-height: 560px'] > div[style*='FFF3B0'] span{visibility:hidden}",
  "artboardRemove": [],
  "pageRemove": [],
  "budget": 1.6,
  "budgetReason": "Below the suggestion card the page keeps the reader's switcher list and 'Checked on this page (n)' fold where the canvas draws a checked row and a flag button; the source line lacks the words after the dot (no API field). Every box above that is probed and matches. The toolbar chips and the card buttons are 52px boxes (the 52px rule, measured by e2e) where the board draws 44px and 49px, which adds about 0.1%."
